          "figure_id": "FIG1",
          "general_description": "Hepatic laboratory course during the captioned second hospitalization and outpatient follow-up.",
          "detailed_description": "One line chart on a white background has title Evolution of Main Hepatic Function Parameters, faint gray dotted grid lines and a boxed nine-item legend at upper right. Five equally spaced columns read Admission, Day 3, Day 7, Day 14, Day 28 (outpatient). The yellow ALT and green AST curves descend from near 2000 and 1650 to roughly 575 and 450. The black LDH line descends from about 575 to 300 and ends at Day 14. Dark-blue GGT and orange-red ALP stay near 175-to-225 with small changes. Gold/orange, light-blue and pink low-valued curves are close to the baseline and partly overlap. Circular point markers match line colors. The y axis combines U/L, mg/dL, g/L and INR on one linear 0-to-2000 scale. There are no panel letters, arrows, treatment-dose labels or individually printed laboratory point values.",
